* string_concat -- grows a string one character at a time and reports its length.
* bottleneck: string growth; cost rises with length.
* batch PINNED (batch=20000 below): this kernel's cost per iteration is not steady-state,
* so the batch size is part of the workload and must not float.
* Standalone:  scrip string_concat.sno   |   sbl -bf string_concat.sno
        &TRIM = 1
        &ANCHOR = 0
        &STLIMIT = -1
        DEFINE('STRING_CONCAT(N)')                      :(STRING_CONCAT_END)
STRING_CONCAT  S = ''
        ZI = 1
ZBL     S = S 'x'
        ZI = LT(ZI, N) ZI + 1                           :S(ZBL)
        STRING_CONCAT = SIZE(S)                         :(RETURN)
STRING_CONCAT_END
*BENCH kernel=STRING_CONCAT check=1000 bud=500 flr=20 batch=20000
        OUTPUT = 'length after 10 appends = ' STRING_CONCAT(10)
        OUTPUT = 'length after 1000 appends = ' STRING_CONCAT(1000)
END
